sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: 3C serialisation: one branch at a time, at two levels
  accDescr: Within a milestone, /3c-project-manager deliver resolves the milestone name exactly, fetches the open issues, states their dependency order and count, runs sprint readiness, then delivers each issue through stages 1 to 5 and opens the next branch only after the previous PR has merged. Across projects, /3c-programme-manager deliver orders the projects with 3c deps order, runs /3c-project-manager for each one, asks a person before the next project, and stops before the dependents of a project whose verdict is blocking.
  autonumber
  participant P as Person
  participant PGM as /3c-programme-manager
  participant PM as /3c-project-manager
  participant GH as GitHub

  rect rgb(238, 242, 255)
  Note over P,GH: Within a milestone: /3c-project-manager deliver
  P->>PM: deliver a milestone
  PM->>GH: resolve the milestone name
  alt no exact match
    PM-->>P: refuse, never run the name as typed
  else exact match
    PM->>GH: fetch the open issues
    PM-->>P: dependency order and issue count
    PM->>PM: sprint readiness: enrichment and coherence
    loop each issue, in dependency order
      PM->>PM: stages 1 to 5, a person confirms branch and PR
      GH-->>PM: PR merged, only then the next branch
    end
  end
  Note right of PM: blocking after one fix cycle stops the batch.<br/>An unclear AC skips that issue only.
  end

  rect rgb(254, 243, 199)
  Note over P,GH: Across projects: /3c-programme-manager deliver
  P->>PGM: deliver
  PGM->>PGM: 3c deps order
  loop each project, in dependency order
    PGM->>PM: run the pipeline for the project's issue
    alt blocking verdict
      PM-->>PGM: blocking
      PGM-->>P: stop before its dependents
    else delivered
      PM-->>PGM: delivered
      PGM-->>P: confirm before the next project
    end
  end
  end
